      "value": "paternal_RF-EMR_exposure_may_affect_fetal_growth_and_placental_efficiency_through_sperm-mediated_epigenetic_mechanisms",
      "verification_status": "reported",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "block_id": "b00027",
          "quote": "We previously showed that 10-week paternal RF-EMR exposure predisposes male offspring to impaired glucose metabolism in a mouse model (Yan et al., 2022). However, whether chronic paternal Wi-Fi exposure influences intrauterine development through sperm-mediated epigenetic mechanisms remains to be determined."
        }
      ]
